<title>BANGLADESH: Clashes halt cargo handling at Bangladeshi port.</title>
<headline>Clashes halt cargo handling at Bangladeshi port.</headline>
<dateline>CHITTAGONG, Bangladesh 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fighting erupted between workers backed by rival political parties at Bangladesh's main port on Friday, injuring 20 and halting cargo handling, police said.</p>
<p>The police said fighting broke out in the southeastern port city of Chittagong when a march staged by members of the pro-government Jatiya Dock Sramik League to demand early union elections came under attack from workers backed by the opposition Bangladesh Nationalist Party.</p>
<p>Port officials said cargo handling had been suspended at the port beginning at 1200 GMT as the rival workers clashed.</p>
<p>&quot;Sporadic clashes are still continuing. We are making efforts to calm the fighting workers,&quot; a port official said.</p>
<p>The officials said 13 ships were in port when the unrest broke out.</p>
</text>
